  "notes": "Piano solo on ONE grand staff (brace). A correct conversion yields exactly ONE part \"Piano\" with 2 staves; it must NOT be split into right/left hand parts, and the second right-hand voice in bars 13-16 must stay inside the piano part (voice 2), not become a new part. DAMAGE (crop): Image edges cut through the staves. Mild: tight crop 0.4 mm outside the staff ends (braces/brackets cut off), header kept. Scan: header (title/credits) cropped away, -1.06 mm cut into the staff starts and 3.0 mm off the staff ends (end barlines gone). Severe: cut -0.96 mm into the staff starts (up to just before the first clef / part name / lyric) and 6.32 mm off the ends (to just after the right-most notehead/stem/lyric). Cut amounts are computed per page from the clean raster so that no clef, key/time signature, notehead, stem, accidental, lyric or part name is removed - only staff-line ends, brackets/braces, barlines and the header. TRUTH LIMITATIONS: Barlines at system starts/ends (incl. the final barline) are partly or completely cut off - they are still present in the truth. scan/severe: title/composer/poet header text is not visible; ignore work-title/creators when scoring."
 },
